# EXVS2 JSON Artifact Isolation

The cross-agent hub is `AGENTS.md`; read it before using `exvs2-json`.

- Put every persisted artifact created while preparing, running, or validating
  `exvs2-json` under the repository-root `tmp/` directory.
- Prefer `tmp/exvs2-json/<task>/` so artifacts from separate investigations do
  not collide.
- Covered artifacts include redirected `inspect` and `correlate` JSON, edit
  request JSON, `edit --output` binaries, reports, logs, diffs, and manually
  created round-trip fixtures.
- Treat source assets as read-only inputs. Never place an output beside an input
  or directly modify an input unless the user explicitly requests that exact
  destructive operation.
- Do not persist these artifacts in `docs/`, `src-tauri/`, another source tree,
  or the repository root.
- From the repository root, use `tmp/...`; from `src-tauri/`, use `../tmp/...`.
- Console-only output is not a file artifact. If it must be retained, redirect
  it to a file under `tmp/`.
- `tmp/` is gitignored. Do not force-add generated artifacts to version control.

Example from `src-tauri/`:

```powershell
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force "..\tmp\exvs2-json\<task>" | Out-Null
.\target\debug\exvs2_json.exe inspect "<input>" --summary --pretty |
  Out-File -Encoding utf8 "..\tmp\exvs2-json\<task>\inspect.json"
```
